<title>UK: U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</title>
<headline>U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total 45,400 tonnes of current series white sugar received export rebates of a maximum 47.002 European Currency Units (Ecus) per 100 kilos at Wednesday's European Union (EU) tender, the U.K. Intervention Board said.</p>
<p>Out of this, traders in France received 26,900 tonnes, in the U.K. 10,000 and in Belgium 8,500 tonnes, it added.  </p>
<p>Earlier on Wednesday, London traders had expected the subsidy for the current season whites campaign for licences to be between 47.000 and 47.002 Ecus per 100 kilos.</p>
<p>Traders had also forecast the total authorised sugar tonnage export awards to be between 70,000 and 100,000 tonnes versus 103,150 last week when the restitution was 47.098 Ecus.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
